$ curl -si http://localhost/api/products/cheapest   (otra vez: cache hit, otro nodo)
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
x-request-trace: presentation-lb-master -> webnode1 -> application-lb-master -> app1 -> redis (cache hit)

$ POST reseña con Idempotency-Key: evidencia-0001  → 202 (cola RabbitMQ)
{"status":"accepted","idempotencyKey":"evidencia-0001","sku":"ST-001"}
  HTTP 202
$ mismo POST otra vez (misma llave)
{"status":"accepted","idempotencyKey":"evidencia-0001","sku":"ST-001"}
  HTTP 202

$ curl -s http://localhost/api/products/ST-001/reviews   (una sola reseña "Evidencia")
            "reviewer": "Evidencia",
            "comment": "Guardada por el worker desde RabbitMQ",
            "comment": "Sturdy and convenient for grocery shopping.",
            "reviewer": "Alex"

$ PUT /api/products/ST-002/price sin token
{"error":"Missing or invalid bearer token"}  HTTP 401
$ PUT /api/products/ST-002/price con token  → catalog.changed
{"sku":"ST-002","price":4.1,"cacheInvalidation":"queued"}  HTTP 200
$ precio de ST-002 después de la invalidación
[{'id': 5, 'sku': 'ST-002', 'name': 'Wooden Pencil Set', 'description': 'Pack of six graphite pencils.', 'price': '4.10'}]

$ rabbitmqctl list_queues name messages consumers
name	messages	consumers
catalog.invalidate	0	2
reviews.retry.1s	0	0
catalog.refresh	0	2
reviews.retry.30s	0	0
reviews.dlq	0	0
reviews.created	0	2
reviews.retry.5s	0	0

$ POST /api/cache/clear  y luego GET (cache miss → un worker repuebla la caché)
{"cacheKey":"store:products:cheapest:v1","cacheEntryRemoved":true,"keysRemoved":1}
x-request-trace: presentation-lb-master -> webnode3 -> application-lb-master -> app2 -> redis (cache miss) -> rabbitmq (catalog.refresh) -> redis (filled by worker)

